{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projection", "label": "Projection (read-side view)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The journal is append-only and authoritative, so projections are derived and can be rebuilt from scratch by replaying it. That decouples write throughput (durable, append-only) from read throughput (denormalized, query-optimized)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "label": "ProjectionActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## A minimal example", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loads its offset cursor on preStart, polls the query layer for events from the cursor onward, calls handle per event, persists the new cursor, repeats."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bytagprojectionoptions", "label": "ByTagProjectionOptions / ProjectionActor.byTag", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## Two query shapes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cursor is an Offset (timestamp + tiebreaker); reads everything carrying a tag across the journal. The common case."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bypersistenceidprojectionoptions", "label": "ByPersistenceIdProjectionOptions / ProjectionActor.byPersistenceId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## Per-pid projections", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cursor is a sequenceNr per persistenceId; one actor per pid, useful for narrow per-entity views. Does not scale to millions of pids - a single tag projection hashing by pid does."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_offsetstore", "label": "OffsetStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## OffsetStore", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores the cursor per projection name + scope. Co-locate it with the read model in production so they crash together, which minimizes the re-processing window."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_inmemoryoffsetstore", "label": "InMemoryOffsetStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## OffsetStore", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default; fine for tests, useless in production because every restart re-processes from the beginning."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_durablestateoffsetstore", "label": "DurableStateOffsetStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## OffsetStore", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wraps any DurableStateStore so offsets survive restarts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_atleastoncedelivery", "label": "At-least-once projection delivery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## At-least-once delivery", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework guarantees no event is missed, but the cursor is persisted after the handler runs, so a crash between the two re-delivers. Duplicates are possible by construction."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_idempotenthandler", "label": "Idempotent handler requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## At-least-once delivery", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without idempotency at-least-once becomes 'occasionally duplicate'. UPSERT rather than blind INSERT, track processed event ids, or use the event's sequenceNr as a per-pid dedup key since it is monotonic per persistenceId. The alternative - a 2-phase commit with the offset save - is not provided out of the box."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "label": "recoveryStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## When the handler throws", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cursor only advances after handle returns, so a failing handler is head-of-line blocking by construction; the strategy only decides how long that lasts. Retries are deferred by retryBackoffMs, doubling to maxRetryBackoffMs, and maxRetries counts attempts after the first."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_retryandfail", "label": "retry-and-fail (default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## When the handler throws", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retries then stops the projection - pick it when a silently stale view is worse than an obviously stopped one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_retryandskip", "label": "retry-and-skip", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## When the handler throws", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retries then steps past the event - pick it when liveness beats completeness (a dashboard, a search index)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_failstopsactor", "label": "`fail` stops the actor rather than escaping the tick", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## When the handler throws", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The projection group's supervisor restarts its children, so an escaping error would reload the same cursor and fail on the same event - a restart loop, louder than the spin it replaced and no more useful. A stopped projection keeps its cursor, so fixing the cause resumes at exactly the failing event."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_onfailure", "label": "onFailure hook", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "### What a failure produces", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Called on every attempt with the offending PersistentEvent, the error, the attempt number and the action taken; this is the structured alerting signal. A hook that throws is logged and swallowed, so a broken reporter cannot take the projection down with it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectiondeadletter", "label": "Skipped event as a DeadLetter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "### What a failure produces", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A skipped event is published on the system event stream wrapped in a DeadLetter naming the projection as recipient, so nothing vanishes without a trace; with no subscriber and the dead-letter queue off, publishing is all that happens."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionmetrics", "label": "Projection failure metrics and logs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "### What a failure produces", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "persistence_projection_stalled / _failures_total / _events_skipped_total, plus one error line when a failure streak opens and one when it ends - the retries in between go to debug, so a projection stuck for a day costs two error lines rather than one per poll."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_pollinterval", "label": "Projection polling (pollIntervalMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## Polling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At idle the cost is one journal query per interval. Lower (250-500 ms) trades database load for propagation latency; higher (5-10 s) is cheap and slow."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_allpersistenceids", "label": "allPersistenceIds fan-out", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "### Fan-out: starting one as each entity appears", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A live stream of every id the journal has seen plus each new one, so per-pid projections can be started as entities appear. The loop never ends (run it in its own task) and one actor per entity is still one actor per entity - for millions of short-lived ones, a tag projection is the answer."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_multipleprojections", "label": "Many projections over one journal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## Multiple projections, same journal", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each has its own offset cursor and reads independently - one event stream, many derived views, none coupled to the other. This is the strength of event sourcing."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bytagprojectionoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bypersistenceidprojectionoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_offsetstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_offsetstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_inmemoryoffsetstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_offsetstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_durablestateoffsetstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_atleastoncedelivery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_atleastoncedelivery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_idempotenthandler", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_retryandfail", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_retryandskip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_failstopsactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_onfailure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_retryandskip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectiondeadletter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_recoverystrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionmetrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projectionactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_pollinterval", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bypersistenceidprojectionoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_allpersistenceids", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_multipleprojections", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_projection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_bytagprojectionoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_tagsfor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## Two query shapes", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_inmemoryoffsetstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshot_stores_in_memory_inmemorysnapshotstore", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## OffsetStore", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_idempotenthandler", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_deterministiccommutativecontract", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "## At-least-once delivery", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_projections_onfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_snapshots_retentionbesteffort", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/projections.mdx", "source_location": "### What a failure produces", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}